    "q-95999": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95999",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$\\int (-\\operatorname{sech}⁡t\\operatorname{tanh}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡t)=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡t\\operatorname{tanh}⁡t\\,⇒\\,\\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡t\\operatorname{tanh}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡t+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (-\\operatorname{sech}⁡t\\operatorname{tanh}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-\\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡t\\operatorname{tanh}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡t)+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sech}⁡t+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
