      "dom_id": "step-q96010",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$\\int (-{sech}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡t)={sech}^{2}⁡t\\,⇒\\,\\int {sech}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=\\operatorname{tanh}⁡t+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (-{sech}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-\\int {sech}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡t+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
